Workflows 

The Security HIVE system, currently, supports two independent workflows: 

SNOW data onboarding workflow: An ETL pipeline designed specifically for onboarding, processing and loading ServiceNow datasets to the HIVE destination system. 

MOBIUS data onboarding workflow: An ETL pipeline dedicated to onboarding, processing, and loading MOBIUS datasets to the HIVE destination system.  

CSAM data onboarding workflow: An ETL pipeline dedicated to onboarding, processing, and loading MOBIUS datasets to the HIVE destination system.    

AXONIUS data onboarding workflow: An ETL pipeline dedicated to onboarding, processing, and loading AXONIUS datasets to HIVE destination system.  

POAM Audit Controls Tred Workflow: A dedicated pipeline for extracting POAM Audit  Controls data from multiple source tables, consolidating the information, and appending it to a historical table  

Data Onbaording Pipelines Actions  

All Security HIVE data onbaording workflows take the following pipeline action to  efficiently ingest, process, and store data while ensuring data quality and compliance with business requirements. 

get raw glue job:  

Ingests external data and stores it in the S3 raw bucket in parquet format  

process glue job: 

Retrieves raw data from the S3 raw bucket 

Applies relevant data quality and business rules to clean and enrich records in the datasets  

Classifies records into three categories based on data quality and business rule validation: 

Clean: Records that pass all data quality checks and comply fully with business rules, ensuring they are error-free and ready for downstream processing. 

Quarantine: Records that contain errors or violate data quality standards or business rules, requiring further review or remediation. 

Warning: Records that do not fail outright but exhibit anomalies or inconsistencies that warrant further investigation 

Loads datasets into the S3 processed bucket according to their classification 

load glue job: 

Retrieves data from the S3 processed storage 

Validates referential integrity of records  

Loads datasets into the target RDS database tables, using `DEFERABLE on FK ` loading strategy to ensure relational integrity of datasets, following the following three stages:  

Load  

Create temp tables – staged tables  

Load the clean data into staged tables  

Create temp table for orphan records – orphan tables  

Create temp table for staged minus orphan records – compliant tables  

Post-Load (single transaction w/ deferred constraint checks)  

Truncate the base tables   

Insert data from compliant tables into base tables  

Insert data from orphan tables into quarantine table  

Refresh materialized views  

Commit transaction  

On commit failure or constraint violation  

All changes made in commit will be rolled back to state before commit was made. 

normalize glue job: 

Accesses clean data from the target database 

Parses and extracts fields where necessary  

Generates records for derived datasets based on business requirements 

Loades the generated tables to the target database 

 

Workflow Steps 

 

Historical Data mainitaining Pipelines Actions 

A single AWS Glue job is responsible for managing the historical data pipeline. This job extracts data from the designated source tables and loads it into the destination historical table. Throughout the process, the pipeline ensures that only a single copy of each data record is maintained, supporting data integrity and consistency in the historical repository. 

